---
const repoUrl = "https://github.com/mgzwarrior/mgz-pkmn";
const discussionsUrl = "https://github.com/mgzwarrior/mgz-pkmn/discussions";
---

<section
  id="why"
  class="border-b border-sand-300 dark:border-husk-200/80 px-6 py-20 sm:py-24"
>
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_15rem] lg:items-start">
    <div>
    <p
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-sand-300 bg-sand-100 backdrop-blur px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-coconut-500 dark:border-husk-50 dark:bg-husk-200/60 dark:text-sand-200"
    >
      <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-palm-400 dark:bg-sun-300"></span>
      From the maker
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-6 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-coconut-700 dark:text-sand-50 text-balance"
    >
      Why I built this.
    </h2>

    <div
      class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-coconut-500 dark:text-sand-200"
    >
      <p>
        I'm Matt — a collector who writes software. mgz-pkmn started with my own
        binders: I'd map out the collection I wanted, then get the order wrong,
        miscount, miss a card, and never quite see where the gaps were. What I
        wanted was one clean list — the cards I'm chasing, with current prices —
        to carry into a show and set in front of a vendor.
      </p>
      <p>
        So I built it, in the hours around a full-time engineering job. Becoming
        a parent pulled me further into the hobby, not out of it — and into the
        community around it.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's collector-first, and built by a real collector for real collectors.
        The market's been pulled around by speculation and big money, and plenty
        of people got priced out of their own hobby. This is the opposite bet:
        make Pokemon accessible to everyone — whatever your age, budget, or reason
        for collecting.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's MIT-licensed and built in the open — and yes, there's an Exeggutor or
        two hiding in it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a
        href={repoUrl}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-sand-100 backdrop-blur px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-coconut-700 hover:bg-sand-200 hover:border-sand-400 dark:border-husk-50 dark:bg-husk-200/60 dark:text-sand-50 dark:hover:bg-husk-100 dark:hover:border-coconut-400 transition"
      >
        See the code
      </a>
      <a
        href={discussionsUrl}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-palm-500 hover:text-palm-400 dark:text-sun-300 dark:hover:text-sun-200"
      >
        Tell me what's missing →
      </a>
    </div>
    </div>

    {/* The favorite — Southern Islands Exeggutor, fittingly tropical. */}
    <figure class="mx-auto w-40 sm:w-48 lg:mx-0 lg:w-full lg:max-w-[15rem]">
      <img
        src="/cards/si1-13.webp"
        alt="Exeggutor, Southern Islands 13"
        width="600"
        height="825"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rotate-3 rounded-lg shadow-xl shadow-coconut-700/20 ring-1 ring-sand-300/60 dark:shadow-black/40 dark:ring-white/10"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-sand-500 dark:text-sand-400">
        Exeggutor · Southern Islands
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
